# Colab Notebook Migration Rules

When updating the remote Colab notebook (Barnett_Cottereau_Zhang_Assignment2_COLAB.ipynb), follow these rules:

## Path Rules
- All data paths must use `/content/drive/MyDrive/data` as the base path
- Model save paths must use `/content/drive/MyDrive/` (e.g., `/content/drive/MyDrive/task2_best_model.pth`)
- Submission file must be saved to `/content/drive/MyDrive/task2_submission.csv`
- Test indices must be saved to `/content/drive/MyDrive/task2_test_indices.npy`

## DataLoader Configuration
- All DataLoader instances must use `num_workers=2` (Colab requirement)
- Remove `persistent_workers=True` and `pin_memory=True` (not needed in Colab)
- Remove `prefetch_factor` parameter (not needed in Colab)

## GPU Optimization
- Remove all GPU optimization code:
  - Remove `torch.backends.cudnn.benchmark` settings
  - Remove `torch.backends.cudnn.deterministic` settings
  - Remove mixed precision training code (`torch.amp.autocast`, `GradScaler`)
  - Remove `non_blocking=True` from `.to(device)` calls
  - Remove `use_amp` flags and conditional logic
  - Simplify device setup to: `device = torch.device('cuda' if torch.cuda.is_available() else 'cpu')`
  - Remove all GPU detection print statements (Colab handles this automatically)

## Code Structure
- All dataset classes must be defined inline in the notebook (no imports from datasets.py)
- All functions must be defined inline in the notebook
- Keep the same cell structure and organization as the original notebook
- Maintain markdown cells for section headers

## File Creation
- Do NOT create any files except the submission CSV file
- Model checkpoints should be saved to Google Drive (`/content/drive/MyDrive/`)
- Do NOT create directories like `@generated-data/` - use Google Drive instead

## Google Drive Mount
- First cell must mount Google Drive: `from google.colab import drive; drive.mount('/content/drive')`
- Assume data is already in `/content/drive/MyDrive/data/kaggle_challenge/`

## Submission Generation
- Submission generation code must:
  1. Load the best model from `/content/drive/MyDrive/task2_best_model.pth`
  2. Use Test551 dataset for Kaggle test set
  3. Generate predictions and convert to label names
  4. Save to `/content/drive/MyDrive/task2_submission.csv`

## General Notes
- Keep code simple and straightforward - Colab handles GPU optimization automatically
- Remove any Windows-specific optimizations or workarounds
- Ensure all imports are present in the imports cell
- Maintain the same training logic and hyperparameters as the local version

